backups/

# Android TWA signing keys — never commit
*.jks
*.keystore
apps/web/twa/android-keystore.jks

# --- Android TWA: ignore the build output, never the project -----------------
#
# This block used to ignore `apps/web/twa/app/` — the Gradle *module source*
# (AndroidManifest.xml, the Java classes, every `res/` file) — along with
# `gradle/`, `gradlew`, `gradlew.bat`, `build.gradle`, `settings.gradle` and
# `gradle.properties`. The result was that `git ls-files apps/web/twa` returned
# only the README and `twa-manifest.json`, while
# `.github/workflows/android-twa.yml` claimed to build "from the committed
# Bubblewrap project": nothing under the Android tree had ever been reviewed or
# could be reproduced from a clone. `bubblewrap update` calls
# `TwaGenerator.removeTwaProject()` and then regenerates the whole module from
# the CLI's bundled template, so the next release would also have replaced
# whatever was on disk — the ignore rule was protecting a source tree from
# being committed and simultaneously guaranteeing it would be overwritten.
#
# The correct ignore is the *output* directory. Bubblewrap and Gradle write
# everything they produce under a `build` directory — `app/build/` for the
# module, `build/` at the project root (the generic `build/` rule above already
# matches both at any depth; the explicit line below keeps that true for someone
# reading only this block) — and `.gradle/` for the Gradle daemon's local state.
# `apps/web/twa/app/src/**`, `apps/web/twa/app/build.gradle`,
# `apps/web/twa/build.gradle`, `apps/web/twa/settings.gradle`,
# `apps/web/twa/gradle.properties`, the `gradle/` wrapper (jar + properties) and
# `gradlew` / `gradlew.bat` are the project, and are committed on purpose.
apps/web/twa/app/build/
apps/web/twa/build/
apps/web/twa/.gradle/

# Signed and unsigned build artifacts. `app-release-bundle.aab` had no rule at
# all before this, so the one output the Play upload path exists to produce was
# the only one that could have been committed by accident.
*.apk
*.apk.idsig
*.aab

# Bubblewrap records the SHA-1 of the `twa-manifest.json` it last generated the
# project from, and `bubblewrap build` compares it: when the file is missing or
# stale it stops and asks whether to regenerate. The release workflow writes it
# before building, and it is derived from a committed file, so it is generated
# state rather than source.
apps/web/twa/manifest-checksum.txt

# The Play Store listing icon Bubblewrap leaves beside the project. Nothing in
# the Gradle project or the manifest references it (the icons the APK actually
# carries are generated into `app/src/main/res/mipmap-*`), so it is an upload
# artifact, not source.
apps/web/twa/store_icon.png

# playwright (root)
test-results/
.design-sync

